From: BAR macOS port
Subject: [PATCH] zink: enable renderpass tracking/optimization for KosmicKrisp

*** STATUS: SHIPPED in v0.12 (moved from patches/mesa-candidates/ on 2026-07-23
*** per user decision). Certified before inclusion: long1 Air A/B +4.8% (fresh
*** interleaved n=3/arm, clean separation, every rp run > every control run) /
*** ~+5.6% aggregate with the earlier n=3; determinism BIT-EXACT (fixed-seed
*** DumpState, 0-diff 94802-line sim dump); testcard contamination 0. Applies
*** clean as patch 0013 of the 12+1 series on pinned mesa 8f272b1fe1.

KosmicKrisp is a tile-based (TBDR) Vulkan driver on Apple GPUs, exactly
like Honeykrisp and the other tilers already listed in zink's
"these drivers benefit from renderpass optimization" switch. It was the
only tile-based driver omitted, so zink left renderpass tracking OFF for
it by default.

With tracking off, zink cannot coalesce the load/store actions of
adjacent color-only and color+depth passes, so each frame incurs extra
full-resolution tile load/store round-trips (each a full tile
store+reload on a TBDR GPU). Adding KOSMICKRISP to the list merges those
passes (measured on M2: ~20 -> ~11.5 render-encoder round-trips/frame,
submits 44 -> 28/s), ~5% less GPU time per frame, with byte-identical
output (this is the same code path already validated on Honeykrisp and
turnip, and is exactly what ZINK_DEBUG=rp toggles).

Render-only change: it does not touch the synchronized simulation, so it
is determinism-neutral (verified bit-exact via DumpState).

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -3086,6 +3086,7 @@ init_driver_workarounds(struct zink_screen *screen)
    case VK_DRIVER_ID_BROADCOM_PROPRIETARY:
    case VK_DRIVER_ID_ARM_PROPRIETARY:
    case VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_HONEYKRISP:
+   case VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_KOSMICKRISP:
       screen->driver_workarounds.track_renderpasses = true; //screen->info.primgen_feats.primitivesGeneratedQueryWithRasterizerDiscard
       break;
    default:
